{"name":"Cool Avocado","hex":"#c4b47d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cool","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a mildly low temperature.","Allowing or suggesting heat relief."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A moderate or refreshing state of cold; moderate temperature of the air between hot and cold; coolness.","A calm temperament."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cool"},{"term":"avocado","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The large, usually yellowish-green or black, savory fruit of the avocado tree.","The avocado tree, Persea americana, of the laurel family."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a dull yellowish-green colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/avocado"}],"entries":[{"title":"Avocado","blocks":[{"text":"The avocado, alligator pear or avocado pear is an evergreen tree in the laurel family (Lauraceae). It is native to the Americas, with archaeological evidence of early human avocado use dating back thousands of years across various regions of Central and South America. It was prized for its large and unusually oily fruit. The native range of avocado extends from Mexico to Peru, encompassing much of Central America and parts of northern and western South America."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Persea_americana_fruit_2.JPG/330px-Persea_americana_fruit_2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Avocado"},{"title":"Shades of chartreuse","blocks":[{"text":"Shades of chartreuse are listed below. Chartreuse is a color between yellow and green, so named because of its resemblance to the color of the French liqueur green chartreuse."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Shades_of_chartreuse_%28x25%29.svg/330px-Shades_of_chartreuse_%28x25%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://